      "record": {
        "id": "dispatch-incident-halt-is-never-downgraded",
        "statement": "A dispatch halt declared as a P1 incident outranks a capacity pause on the same target: a later capacity pause replaces neither its source, its reason nor its declarer, and only an operator lifts it. A capacity pause lifts itself after two consecutive clear reconciler rounds.",
        "contexts": [
          "run"
        ],
        "examples": [
          "The orphan threshold trips while a P1 holds the pool: the halt stays a P1 with the responder's reason.",
          "A P1 arrives while a capacity pause holds a node: the halt becomes the P1 and names the responder.",
          "Leaks stay below the threshold for two rounds: the capacity pause lifts, while a P1 on the same target stays."
        ],
